\ Temporary bridge from a native signed CAL day into an exact
\ signed-wide day. The destination is a wide signed day record.
\ The native minimum -2147483648 cannot be negated within a signed
\ 32-bit number, so this bridge refuses that one input explicitly.
\ The full calendar still uses the stricter temporary safety bounds.
\ Arbitrary-wide dates do not pass through this bridge.

The converted signed day result is a wide signed day.
The native widening succeeded is a number.

\ One-token scratch names avoid CAL-4018 treating an embedded type name
\ as an undeclared type (as confirmed by the v080 native diagnostic).
The bridgeabsolute is a calendar day.
The bridgepolarity is a number.
The bridgemagnitude is a wide quantity.

To convert a calendar day into a wide signed day:
  Put 0 into the native widening succeeded.
  If the calendar day is less than -2147483647, exit.
  Put the calendar day into the bridgeabsolute.
  Put 1 into the bridgepolarity.
  If the bridgeabsolute is less than 0,
    multiply -1 by the bridgeabsolute;
    put -1 into the bridgepolarity.
  Convert the bridgeabsolute to a string.
  Put the string into the bridgemagnitude.
  Set the converted signed day result from the bridgemagnitude given the bridgepolarity.
  Put 1 into the native widening succeeded.
